{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791838708,"nonce":"FETJlimqS6YzgDuXzIUzIStxaeo=","message":"Checkpoint 5 completed for the supported standalone prototype in 038b24b458e5ffb808e87c0463567cc1ba5f2cbf.\n\nFixed a validation/activation defect: ASH_AIR_NO_INLINE also hid callee bodies from the legality checker, so attempts to keep generated calls visible could silently disable fusion. TreeModule now exposes proof_body independently of inlining policy; Ash supplies raw lowered bodies while keeping its normal inliner gates intact. Runtime contract checks are unchanged. Tests verify that withholding inliner bodies does not prevent proof, and unknown allocation policy still refuses helper construction.\n\nNew executable coverage:\n- TestTreeFusionMatrix: unary/ternary topologies, depth argument positions, reordered fields and child consumption, constructor negation, a Haxe-inline wrapper and 128 deterministic wrapping-integer cases. Retained trees supply the unfused reference. Four sites / two helpers. Output tree-matrix=-663667236 agrees with optimization off/on across interpreter, Cranelift, LLVM and hybrid under ASH_GC_STRESS=17, ASH_GC_VERIFY_HEAP=1 and ASH_VERIFY_AIR=1. Collections must exceed the eight explicit requests; a local control has eight without stress versus eleven with stress.\n- Hot matrix mode: a local reference and scalar accumulator survive an asserted OSR entry in the rewritten caller. A separate run disables inlining, pins promotion to the generated helper and asserts Cranelift and LLVM installations (Cranelift only without LLVM). Output agrees with original interpreter, tree-matrix=600733032. Merely running hybrid is not treated as evidence that a transition occurred.\n- TestTreeFusionRefusals: no helpers/sites transform. Exact observable event order, shared/escaping references, identity, mutation, dynamic calls, skipped children, constructor exceptions, consumer exceptions and Null access agree across tiers. Original and fused-option executions of a divergent producer are both bounded/killed after two seconds; stdout is explicitly flushed before entry so a startup timeout cannot count as preserved divergence.\n- TestTreeFusionSuspended: retained local tree survives suspension and explicit collection before/after a fused call, with ASH_WORKERS=0 and 2 across modes. Each checks tree-suspended=57, collection count, and one transformed site/helper.\n- Core policy tests refuse hosted metadata, external native libraries, object/reload registration hooks. Fresh subprocesses install actual object tails, drop policy or layout room and verify active-policy refusal without contaminating other tests. Existing atomic rollback, serialization and reload refusal remain covered.\n\nCommands/results on local macOS arm64:\n- cargo test --offline -p air --lib: 221 passed, including proof negatives and AIR/serialization round trips.\n- cargo test --offline -p ash_core --lib tree_fusion: 3 passed, including three isolated host-policy subprocesses.\n- cargo test --offline -p ash --test tree_fusion_validation --test tree_fusion --test tree_fusion_survey --test generated_helpers -- --nocapture: 15 passed. Portable-helper native AOT execution and wasm object validation still pass.\n- cargo test --offline -p ash --no-default-features --test tree_fusion --test tree_fusion_validation --test tree_fusion_survey: 10 passed. Pre-existing unused write_page warning only.\n- New Rust modules/tests pass rustfmt; git diff --check clean.\n\nUnchanged benchmark checksum -104864 verified by the allocation regression in both build configurations. Source SHA256 d705a3b8c01dd2dcae7a89e27cf814317df8ba50ccbf3ec6d1ea8bfdcfd669b5; bytecode SHA256 9698cecaf8852fa219acfd3361ea8659543cb7dc5a4033168aa3ff96d01a926d. No source, depth or iteration edits.\n\nLimits: local correctness evidence, not CI timing or Linux/Windows validation. Fusion remains opt-in. Fused serialized bytecode/n